### Impact

Heap data race and double free in the recursive-async runtime that `surrealdb-core` uses for every SurrealQL statement (and that SurrealDB's parser, GraphQL lowering and API invocation also use). On the conflicting paths the runtime performs unsynchronised reads/writes of its own `Cell`/`UnsafeCell` allocator state through a shared reference, can drop and deallocate the same type-erased future twice (double free for a heap-owning future), and can hand the same `Option<R>` result to two threads (double ownership). The consequence class is in-process memory corruption in the host Rust process: crash, corrupted results, data disclosure, and in the worst case further exploitation primitives. Availability is already demonstrably affected: the corrupted allocator makes `reblessive` panic (`stack/mod.rs:177:54`) from safe code.

Preconditions (honest scope): a Rust caller must use `reblessive`'s public API in a way the type system currently permits - duplicate a driver future over one `Stack` and poll it from two threads (variant A), or move a `TreeStack`/`Runner` holding a `!Send` capture to another thread (variant B). No remote/black-box trigger was demonstrated, and we found no in-tree call site that does either today; however, `reblessive` is a published crates.io crate (latest 0.4.3, affected) that any Rust project - including any downstream of `surrealdb-core` - can use, and `surrealdb-core`'s own `Send` query futures depend on the unsound assertion. Provisional scoring: `CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H` (High, 7.1); please re-score as you see fit. Weaknesses: CWE-362 (primary), CWE-415 / CWE-416 (secondary).

Suggested remediation: upstream `reblessive` should make `Send`/`Sync` conditional on the erased payload (`Fut: Send`, and drop `Sync` entirely) and/or bind the stepping futures to `&mut Runner`; `FinishFuture`/`StepFuture` should get a `Drop` that restores the stack so cancellation cannot leave dangling tasks. Downstream, keep one `TreeStack` per task/thread and avoid relying on the unconditional `Send`.

### Patches

The unsound `reblessive` dependency has been removed; `surrealdb-core` parses with plain recursion and version 4.0.0 no longer carries the data-race and double-free exposure.

- Version 4.0.0 and later are not affected by this issue.

